At 0 °C the object is really 100 cm away, but the program assumes the sensor works with 343 m/s. What does this code print to the Serial Monitor?

```
float c = 331.3 + 0.606 * 0;       // 0 °C
float okunan = 100.0 * 343.0 / c;
Serial.println(okunan, 1);
```

A student wants to work out the distance from a time of 5830 µs, but the result is a meaningless number instead of centimetres. Which line is wrong?

```
unsigned long sure = 5830;            // µs
float cm = sure * 343.0 / 2.0;
Serial.println(cm);
```
